Feature: Real-time streaming of patient data from S3 to patient_data_auto_loader

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is purgo_databricks and schema is purgo_playground
    And the target table is patient_data_auto_loader with columns:
      | patient_id (string) | patient_name (string) | age (string) | diagnosis (string) | treatment (string) | data_loaded_at (timestamp) |
    And the schema location is "/mnt/checkpoints/s3_autoloader/patient_al_schema"
    And the checkpoint location is "/mnt/checkpoints/patient_al_cp/"
    And Spark S3 access is configured using access_key and secret_key from Databricks secret scope "aws_keys"
    And the S3 folder path is dynamically retrieved from the s3_landing_path column of ingest_config_master where source_object_name contains "patient_data" and active_flag = "Y"
    And the delimiter for CSV is retrieved from the delimiter column of ingest_config_master, defaulting to "," if not present

  Scenario Outline: Stream valid patient data CSV file from S3 and append to patient_data_auto_loader
    Given a new CSV file "<file_name>" arrives in S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the CSV file has columns: patient_id, patient_name, age, diagnosis, treatment
    And all columns are read as String type
    When the streaming job processes the file
    Then a new row is appended to patient_data_auto_loader with:
      | patient_id      | patient_name      | age   | diagnosis      | treatment      | data_loaded_at         |
      | <patient_id>    | <patient_name>    | <age> | <diagnosis>    | <treatment>    | <current_timestamp>    |

    Examples:
      | file_name         | s3_landing_path                | patient_id | patient_name | age | diagnosis   | treatment   |
      | patient_001.csv   | s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/  | P001       | John Smith   | 45  | Diabetes    | Insulin     |
      | patient_002.csv   | s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/  | P002       | Jane Doe     | 38  | Hypertension| Beta Blocker|
      | patient_003.csv   | s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/  | P003       | Alice Lee    | 29  | Asthma      | Inhaler     |

  Scenario: Multiple active patient_data configs in ingest_config_master
    Given ingest_config_master contains multiple rows where source_object_name contains "patient_data" and active_flag = "Y"
    When the streaming job starts
    Then all matching s3_landing_path values are used to monitor for new patient data files

  Scenario: S3 credentials are missing in Databricks secret scope
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the streaming job attempts to access S3
    Then the job fails with error "Missing S3 credentials in secret scope aws_keys"

  Scenario: S3 credentials are invalid
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" contains invalid "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the streaming job attempts to access S3
    Then the job fails with error "Invalid S3 credentials"

  Scenario Outline: CSV file missing required columns
    Given a new CSV file "<file_name>" arrives in S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the CSV file is missing required column "<missing_column>"
    When the streaming job processes the file
    Then the job fails with error "Missing required column <missing_column> in file <file_name>"

    Examples:
      | file_name         | s3_landing_path                | missing_column |
      | patient_004.csv   | s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/  | patient_id     |
      | patient_005.csv   | s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/  | diagnosis      |

  Scenario Outline: CSV file contains type mismatches
    Given a new CSV file "<file_name>" arrives in S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the CSV file has a value "<bad_value>" in column "<column>" that cannot be read as String
    When the streaming job processes the file
    Then the job fails with error "Type mismatch in column <column> for value <bad_value> in file <file_name>"

    Examples:
      | file_name         | s3_landing_path                | column      | bad_value      |
      | patient_006.csv   | s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/  | age         | [binary blob]  |

  Scenario: CSV file with extra columns
    Given a new CSV file "patient_007.csv" arrives in S3 folder "s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/"
    And the CSV file has extra columns not defined in schema
    When the streaming job processes the file
    Then only columns patient_id, patient_name, age, diagnosis, treatment are loaded as String, extra columns are ignored

  Scenario: CSV file with duplicate rows
    Given a new CSV file "patient_008.csv" arrives in S3 folder "s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/"
    And the CSV file contains duplicate rows
    When the streaming job processes the file
    Then all rows are appended to patient_data_auto_loader (no deduplication is performed)

  Scenario: CSV file with empty values
    Given a new CSV file "patient_009.csv" arrives in S3 folder "s3://purgo/patient_data/2024/"
    And the CSV file has empty values in some columns
    When the streaming job processes the file
    Then the corresponding columns in patient_data_auto_loader are set to null

  Scenario: ingest_config_master has no active patient_data config
    Given ingest_config_master has no row where source_object_name contains "patient_data" and active_flag = "Y"
    When the streaming job starts
    Then the job fails with error "No active patient_data config found in ingest_config_master"

  Scenario Outline: Delimiter is not specified in config
    Given ingest_config_master row for patient_data has delimiter column empty
    When the streaming job reads CSV files
    Then the default delimiter "," is used

    Examples:
      | config_id | source_object_name | delimiter |
      | C001      | patient_data_2024  |           |

  Scenario Outline: Delimiter is specified in config
    Given ingest_config_master row for patient_data has delimiter "<delimiter>"
    When the streaming job reads CSV files
    Then delimiter "<delimiter>" is used

    Examples:
      | config_id | source_object_name | delimiter |
      | C002      | patient_data_2024  | ;         |
      | C003      | patient_data_2024  | |         |

  Scenario: Streaming job uses schema location and checkpoint location
    Given the streaming job is configured with schema location "/mnt/checkpoints/s3_autoloader/patient_al_schema"
    And checkpoint location "/mnt/checkpoints/patient_al_cp/"
    When the job runs
    Then schema evolution and state are managed using these locations

  Scenario: data_loaded_at is populated with current timestamp
    Given a new row is appended to patient_data_auto_loader
    When the streaming job processes a patient data record
    Then data_loaded_at is set to the current timestamp at load time

  Scenario: Streaming job continues to append new files
    Given new patient data CSV files continue to arrive in S3
    When the streaming job is running
    Then each new file is appended to patient_data_auto_loader in real time

  Scenario: Streaming job ignores non-patient_data configs
    Given ingest_config_master contains configs where source_object_name does not contain "patient_data"
    When the streaming job starts
    Then those configs are ignored for patient data streaming

  Scenario: Streaming job supports multiple S3 folders for patient_data
    Given ingest_config_master contains multiple active configs for patient_data with different s3_landing_path values
    When the streaming job starts
    Then all specified S3 folders are monitored for new patient data files

# END
